PATCH 186: base-loss + pointer-scaling reconstruction of FUN_0000_2322, the FIRST command handler
dispatched by the in-mission command/script interpreter FUN_0000_22dd (via the patch-185 0a86 cursor).

With patch 185 the 22dd dispatch loop resolves its double-indirection target correctly and calls into
the real handler stream; the first handler is FUN_0000_2322 (a viewport/element geometry setup + a
driver rowtable-pitch method call).  asm 0x2322:
    mov di,[0x156a]     ; di = DAT_1000_d56a  -- a 16-bit DGROUP NEAR-OFFSET to the dest struct
    mov bx,[0x1552]     ; bx = DAT_1000_d552  -- a 16-bit DGROUP NEAR-OFFSET to the src struct
    ... all [di+N]/[bx+N] field reads/writes are DS-relative (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00) ...
    mov ax,[di+4]; lcall [0x55c]   ; call the driver rowtable-pitch method (c55c = mga 0x02c1)

Ghidra typed DAT_1000_d56a `int**` (a 4-byte HOST pointer) and DAT_1000_d552 `undefined2` used as
`*(int*)(d552+N)`, so `DAT_1000_d56a[7] = *(int*)(DAT_1000_d552+0x14)` wild-dereffed the near-offset
as a host address (SIGSEGV).  On top of the base-loss it used Ghidra 2-byte-int element indexing
(`piVar7[7]` = +14 in Ghidra, +28 under gcc), so every field access also doubled its byte offset.

Fix (base-loss/width class, mirrors patches 180/181/182): rebase both structs onto
g_mem+0x1c000+near_offset, read/write uint16 fields at the asm byte offsets, and pass the struct to
its callees (23be, 0d2e, 195d) as the DGROUP OFFSET + segment far-pair the asm forms
(`lea ax/bx,[di]; mov cx,ds`), not a host pointer.  The tail method call `lcall [0x55c]` is threaded
ax = dst[2] (asm `mov ax,[di+4]`).

VALIDATED by driving the ACCEPT cascade (FIST_CASCADE=1 + the patch-172 3-click route, from repo
root): pre-186 the cascade SIGSEGVs inside 2322 at the first field write; post-186 it advances
THROUGH 2322 -- the 22dd loop dispatches, 2322 sets the struct up, and c55c dispatches into the
MGAVIDEO pitch-cache method mga 0x02c1 (which then faults in ITS OWN unrelated linked-list base-loss:
the next frontier).  So 2322 itself now runs crash-free.

Cascade-only / behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows: FUN_0000_2322 has NO direct callers (grep
build/*.c); it is reached ONLY through 22dd's dispatch loop, gated by byte[DGROUP:0x1548]
(DAT_1000_d548) > 0 which is 0 in the menu (verified: 22dd breakpoint shows d548=0 on the menu path).
The pre-patch wild deref would already SIGSEGV the 19 flows if this handler were reached -> they are
19/19.  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu md5 3a6ff1c5 unchanged.  Sources stay pristine
(re_out/fist.c md5 61453e42); fist.c via build/.

